Description: gate examples/.c sed on nodoc so the rule no-ops cleanly
Author: Harkirat S Virk <harkiratsvirk@gmail.com>
Origin: local
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-05-18
Bug-Athena: wpa's execute_after_dh_installexamples runs
 `sed -i debian/*/usr/share/doc/*/examples/*.c` to rewrite
 `#include "includes.h"` → `#include <stddef.h>` (and same for
 wpa_ctrl.h) in the shipped example sources.
 .
 Under DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS=nodoc, dh_installexamples is a no-op, so
 the examples/ directory is never created.  The shell glob expands
 to the literal path, sed errors with
 "can't read debian/*/usr/share/doc/*/examples/*.c: No such file
 or directory" and the build dies.
 .
 Fix: wrap the sed in `ifeq (,$(findstring nodoc,$(DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS)))`
 so the rule no-ops cleanly when nodoc is active.  Behaviour without
 nodoc is unchanged — the sed still rewrites the example includes.
 .
 TEMPORARY: nodoc is a workaround for missing doc-build tooling in
 the build pool, not a permanent policy.  DELETE THIS PATCH when
 CONF-08 lands and nodoc is dropped from [Source] BuildOptions /
 BuildProfiles in config/build.conf.
---
This patch header follows DEP-3: http://dep.debian.net/deps/dep3/
--- a/debian/rules
+++ b/debian/rules
@@ -110,7 +110,9 @@ endif
 ### end dh overrides

 execute_after_dh_installexamples:
+ifeq (,$(findstring nodoc,$(DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS)))
 	sed -e 's="includes.h"=<stddef.h>=' -e 's="common/wpa_ctrl.h"=<wpa_ctrl.h>=' -i debian/*/usr/share/doc/*/examples/*.c
+endif

 %:
 	dh $@
